From cb1551fb1fa6f6759f14134d5b4f9d08eb1ef48b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 17:14:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] prplMesh: fix MLO beacon 11k mode selection, link resolution,
 DM-lifecycle, and BTM flag forwarding

RRM capability is now derived from the STA's own association frame
(active/passive vs table mode) instead of a dead ctrl-iface field,
with an MLD-MAC fallback for MLO clients and a fix for reassociation
frames being misdetected as association requests (which desynced the
IE parse and hid the RM Enabled Capabilities element). Skip the check
entirely for backhaul VAPs. Also fix beacon-report duplication across
overlapping STA reports, an orphaned DM instance when BSSID resolution
fails on disconnect, and link-probe ordering for non-MLD clients.
Default regular-STA beacon measurement to Active with 200 TU duration.

Forward disassoc_imminent and abridged BTM flags from NBAPI
ClientSteering through to the outgoing steering TLV.

sta_beacon_11k_request() picked the preferred link for REQ_BEACON by
probing hostapd's "STA <mac>" ctrl command and stopping at the first
link that reported the STA as associated. For MLO clients, hostapd
reports the STA as associated on every negotiated (setup) link, even
ones that are currently idle and carry no traffic, so this could
resolve to a dormant link before ever reaching the link the STA
actually uses, sending REQ_BEACON where the client isn't listening
(TX status ack=0, no report).

REQ_BEACON is itself a downlink (AP->STA) unicast frame, so the
correct signal is whether the AP has actually delivered traffic to
the STA on a given link (tx_bytes), not RX/SIGNAL, which only
reflects frames received FROM the STA. NL80211 TX_BYTES is also a
cumulative, monotonically-increasing counter, so a bare snapshot
comparison would degrade back to "first link the STA has EVER used"
over time; a per-(link, STA) baseline cache turns that into a delta
since the last check.

The per-link probe used update_stations_stats(), which parses the
flat NL80211_ATTR_STA_INFO attribute directly. The kernel always
fills that attribute from the STA's primary/deflink only
(net/mac80211/sta_info.c sta_set_sinfo()) regardless of which
link_iface is queried, so every probe in the loop returned the same
primary-link snapshot -- confirmed in the field, where three
different links' first-ever probes all reported an identical byte
count within the same few seconds, and the AP's own "iw station
dump" showed one link's per-link stats fully zeroed out while the
top-level aggregate matched the other (real) link's numbers exactly.
Switch the per-link probe to get_sta_info(), which already resolves
the true per-link breakdown from the nested NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINKS
attribute, keyed by the link ID encoded in link_iface, instead of the
primary-link-only flat attribute. Fix a follow-on SMacAddr-to-sMacAddr
conversion bug in this same link-resolution path.

Don't delete the DM STA instance on a stale TOPOLOGY_RESPONSE received
from a former agent.

beerocks_agent_main.cpp reads beacon_11k_{active,passive,table}_measurement_duration
from beerocks_agent.conf and calls bwl::nl80211::set_beacon_11k_*_measurement_duration(),
but those setters only update a process-local static in the bwl library. The 11k
Beacon Request that actually uses those statics is built by mon_wlan_hal_nl80211
running inside the separate fronthaul_manager process, which never received the
configured value and silently fell back to the compiled-in default of 50 TU for
Active requests regardless of what beacon_11k_active_measurement_duration was set
to. Read and apply the same config in Monitor::thread_init(), alongside the
existing beacon_11k_measurement_mode initialization, which already runs in this
same process.

Signed-off-by: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
